Z||000029||Patrick's Dad||05-09-2000||12:20 AM||||geyser... That's exactly what I was thinking. The things that make you go "Hmmm...."<P>Homicidal: One of my wife's tellers had sex once. She now has a daughter. She didn't do it once a month, or once a year. She did it once. Sometimes, we hypocrites are willing to stick our necks out, because we have the benefit of experience. If I tell you, "Don't go rock climbing by yourself." it might be that I once (or more than once) went out climbing rock faces alone, until I slipped and fell well away from anyone, and well before cell phones and arthroscopic surgery were easily available. Does that make me a hypocrite? Maybe. Maybe someone puts thier two cents in because, as a parent, they may be sitting here feeding a two and a half week old, while a four year old resists sleeping, and the clock reads midnight. OTOH, maybe it's sleep deprivation. In either case, thousands of children are abused and neglected every year (A forty minute old baby was recently found in a paper bag by the tire of a person's RAV4 in the parking lot of a closed hospital in Boston), and a million and a half don't make it out of thier mother's body alive (by choice), and maybe a hundred thousand or more unintentionally. So maybe we're worried about the next generation (you), and the one after that. I'll take the moniker of hypocrite, if it means that one person listens. It may be you, it may not, but I'll keep talking. Hopefully, one by one, we'll be better for it.<P>GTB... I'm up for a religion discussion. Or how about politics?<P>Maybe I'll have that feeling tomorrow (this) morning, like someone who got drunk at a party and feels that he may regret some of the things he said. Maybe I won't. It's still a free country, at least (until and if) Algore gets elected....<P>(Sppelng korrektd)<p>[This message has been edited by Patrick's Dad (edited 05-09-2000).]||||reg||1
